<title>UK: Legal &amp; General off on NatWest comments.</title>
<headline>Legal &amp; General off on NatWest comments.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in life assurance group Legal and General fell on Wednesday after analysts at NatWest advised taking profits in the sector.</p>
<p>The shares were off 11p at 376-1/2p by 0859 GMT. Market sources said NatWest had picked Legal and General as the least likely to outperform in the sector.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, others in the sector also slipped and Prudential Corp fell 10p to 536-1/2p.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
